          "publisher": "Apple Music",
          "checked_on": "2026-08-25",
          "note": "Exact Apple Music album page for Derek Gripper's One Night On Earth (Live in Concert)."
        }
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "status": "verified-authoritative-sources",
        "note": "Date, time, venue, billing, personnel and the distinct musical framing of the three performances were verified against NJPAC; Ticketmaster independently confirms the exact function. Repository search found no Mariza, Derek Gripper or matching NJPAC event record before publication. No unannounced collaboration, shared set or additional personnel were inferred."
      },
      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The strength of this bill is adjacency rather than a promised supergroup: Mariza's fado places voice and Portuguese song at the center, Derek Gripper has built a highly individual guitar language by translating African string traditions onto six strings, and Duo Andalus brings voice, oud and flamenco guitar into a Mediterranean and Middle Eastern frame. Hearing those vocabularies consecutively makes the evening a useful map of how song, plucked strings and modal color travel across regions without needing to flatten them into one generic 'world music' sound.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for it if a Newark/NYC trip overlaps the date and fado, guitar language or Mediterranean musical exchange are part of the listening thread. The bill is unusually coherent across very different traditions, but it is best treated as a strong regional night rather than a reason to rebuild a trip by itself.",
          "listen_before": "Mariza — Mundo; Derek Gripper — One Night On Earth (Live in Concert)"
        },
        "es": {
          "why_it_matters": "La fuerza del cartel está en la vecindad de lenguajes, no en prometer un supergrupo: el fado de Mariza pone la voz y la canción portuguesa al centro; Derek Gripper ha construido un lenguaje de guitarra muy personal al trasladar tradiciones africanas de cuerdas a seis cuerdas; y Duo Andalus mete voz, oud y guitarra flamenca dentro de un marco mediterráneo y de Oriente Medio. Escuchar esos vocabularios uno detrás de otro vuelve la noche un mapa muy útil de cómo viajan la canción, las cuerdas pulsadas y el color modal entre regiones sin aplastarlos en una sola etiqueta genérica de 'world music'.",
          "trip_verdict": "Sí le haría espacio activamente si un viaje Newark/NYC coincide con la fecha y el fado, el lenguaje de guitarra o los cruces mediterráneos están en el hilo de escucha. El cartel tiene una coherencia poco común entre tradiciones muy distintas, pero lo trataría como una noche regional fuerte y no como una razón suficiente para rehacer por sí sola todo el viaje.",
          "listen_before": "Mariza — Mundo; Derek Gripper — One Night On Earth (Live in Concert)"
        }
      }
